# Normalize text artifacts to LF in repository and working tree.
# Overrides system-level core.autocrlf for matched patterns.
#
# The catch-all is first because the list below is an allowlist, and two files that
# ship inside the published wheel matched nothing on it: LICENSE and NOTICE land in
# `dist-info/licenses/`. On a Windows checkout they became CRLF (LICENSE 11560 bytes
# against the 11358 stored in git), so a wheel built from a correct checkout of the
# release tag differed from the published one in LICENSE, NOTICE and the RECORD that
# hashes them -- three entries out of 231. Every other entry matched byte for byte,
# which is exactly the shape that makes a reproduction attempt look like tampering.
# Dockerfile, CODEOWNERS and the hash-pinned requirement files were uncovered for the
# same reason.
#
# `text=auto` leaves git's binary detection alone, and no tracked blob currently holds
# a CRLF, so this normalises the working tree without rewriting a single blob.
*           text=auto eol=lf

*.md        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.rego      text eol=lf
*.cel       text eol=lf
.gitignore  text eol=lf
